------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled segmentation tool and model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-totalsegmentator wraps TotalSegmentator and redistributes its pretrained
weights (baked into the published container image). Each remains under its own
license and carries its own citation requirements; if you use the results in
research, please cite the underlying methods (see the "Citation" section of
README.md).

  - TotalSegmentator (segment_anatomy) — anatomical structure segmentation on
    CT and MR images.
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/wasserth/TotalSegmentator
    Cite: Wasserthal et al., "TotalSegmentator: Robust Segmentation of 104
    Anatomic Structures in CT Images", Radiology: Artificial Intelligence 5(5)
    (2023). doi:10.1148/ryai.230024
    For MR tasks additionally cite: D'Antonoli et al., "TotalSegmentator MRI:
    Robust Sequence-independent Segmentation of Multiple Anatomic Structures in
    MRI", Radiology 314(2) (2025). doi:10.1148/radiol.241613

  - nnU-Net (the segmentation engine TotalSegmentator builds on).
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet
    Cite: Isensee et al., "nnU-Net: a self-configuring method for deep
    learning-based biomedical image segmentation", Nature Methods 18:203-211
    (2021). doi:10.1038/s41592-020-01008-z

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope of the redistributed weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TotalSegmentator's code is Apache-2.0, but its pretrained weights are NOT
uniformly so. This image bundles ONLY the tasks whose weights upstream publishes
under Apache-2.0 ("Openly available for any usage" in the upstream README), which
are served as public GitHub release assets.

Deliberately NOT bundled, and not reachable from the tools:

  - Tasks requiring a TotalSegmentator license number (free for non-commercial
    use, paid for commercial use), whose weights are served from the upstream
    license backend: heartchambers_highres, appendicular_bones(_mr),
    tissue_types(_mr), tissue_4_types, brain_structures, face(_mr),
    thigh_shoulder_muscles(_mr), coronary_arteries(_LEGACY), aortic_sinuses,
    renal_arteries, aorta_annulus, aortic_dissection,
    pulmonary_artery_landmarks.
    Licensing: https://backend.totalsegmentator.com/license-academic/

  - brain_aneurysm, which is CC BY-NC 4.0 with no commercial license available.
    Note that upstream does not list this task in `commercial_models`, so it is
    excluded by name rather than by that flag.

The exclusion policy is implemented in
src/medmcp_totalsegmentator/tools/_catalog.py and asserted by
tests/test_licensing.py, which also verifies that every bundled weights URL
points at the public GitHub release rather than the license backend.

Individual TotalSegmentator tasks carry additional citation requirements for the
datasets or papers they derive from; see the upstream README's task list.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled libraries
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python libraries redistributed inside the container image — including
PyTorch, nnU-Net, SimpleITK, nibabel, and their transitive dependency closure —
each remain under their own license; the full license texts travel with each
package's distribution.
